WEBVTT

00:08.360 --> 00:11.280
Aren't the planes themselves straight out of museums?

00:11.280 --> 00:13.960
AWACS: Airborne early-Warning And Control System

00:11.280 --> 00:13.960
For the most part, even if it is an AWACS,

00:13.960 --> 00:16.740
This guy's just a prototype - a pre-modification model!

00:16.780 --> 00:18.240
There's no helping it is there?

00:18.320 --> 00:22.420
After the "Great Lost" these are the best eyes we have left.

00:22.420 --> 00:25.680
It's doing a fine job reading the difficult situation up there.

00:25.680 --> 00:27.220
Pipe down and do your job.

00:27.220 --> 00:28.160
Roger.

00:28.160 --> 00:30.160
Bugbear to First Strike Team,

00:30.160 --> 00:33.320
Presently, we are holding 200 miles from target location,

00:33.320 --> 00:34.340
Observing radar...

00:34.340 --> 00:36.720
No contact, conditions green.

00:36.720 --> 00:38.600
I repeat, conditions--

00:39.320 --> 00:44.700
Look, what I'm trying to say is, to Tatiana, the best plane has definitely got to be the Yak-9P!

00:44.700 --> 00:47.380
In addition to being smaller than Japanese Zero Fighters,

00:47.380 --> 00:51.680
It comes equipped with the powerful, liquid-cooled piston M-107 engine.

00:51.680 --> 00:53.820
Admired on battlefields all over the world,

00:53.820 --> 00:56.860
It was the Kalashnikov of piston engine planes!

00:56.860 --> 00:59.700
And how would you excuse said engine's durability?

00:59.700 --> 01:00.680
Well... that's...

01:00.680 --> 01:04.980
I believe the best plane with a reciprocating engine to be the Avia S-199.

01:04.980 --> 01:08.020
Wait, isn't that just a cheap knock-off of the Bf 109?

01:08.020 --> 01:10.020
The engine is no good.

01:10.020 --> 01:13.420
Engine problems and the like mean nothing to a skilled pilot.

01:13.420 --> 01:15.920
Says the one who just brought up the durability!

01:15.920 --> 01:18.580
Tatiana can't accept that at all!

01:19.960 --> 01:22.700
Tatiana and Noa sure are getting along well!

01:22.700 --> 01:24.580
Christina-senpai!

01:24.580 --> 01:26.740
I'd prefer that you didn't put us together!

01:24.580 --> 01:26.740
Please don't lump me in with someone like her.

01:26.740 --> 01:28.440
See, you guys are matching perfectly!

01:28.440 --> 01:30.440
You're wrong!

01:28.440 --> 01:30.440
I said you're wrong!

01:31.620 --> 01:35.100
Light chitchat while flying 20 feet above sea level...

01:35.100 --> 01:36.360
As one would expect.

01:36.640 --> 01:38.600
Bugbear to Strike Leader,

01:38.600 --> 01:42.720
Just now, we picked up some kind of girl's school canteen like chitchat...

01:42.720 --> 01:44.940
This is Strike Leader Olivia.

01:44.960 --> 01:47.620
Apologies. I switched to the open channel.

01:47.620 --> 01:50.700
So you're saying that just now wasn't interference?

01:50.920 --> 01:52.820
Just who are those fledglings?

01:52.820 --> 01:53.800
Fledglings?

01:55.320 --> 01:57.520
Surely you must have heard of them before:

01:58.000 --> 02:00.820
307 Fighter Squadron of the Chofu Base.

02:01.180 --> 02:03.280
307 Squadron!?

02:03.280 --> 02:04.720
You can't mean that-

02:04.720 --> 02:07.640
Yes. That "Hell Alice".

02:07.640 --> 02:09.840
So that means the super Ace "Ice Doll" is also...

02:10.560 --> 02:12.040
Yeah, she's here as well.

02:18.700 --> 02:20.700
OP

02:28.690 --> 02:33.990
Third Girls Fighter Wing

02:33.820 --> 02:38.890
If I fly beautifully, praise me as I am

02:38.890 --> 02:41.270
Blue, so blue

02:41.270 --> 02:44.380
Being held by such a sky becomes a sin

02:44.380 --> 02:49.340
"GOODBYE" always accelerates hopelessly

02:49.340 --> 02:54.180
This stolen world of ours is Lonely in Blue

02:54.840 --> 02:59.030
If you don't want to give up,

02:59.030 --> 03:04.360
You are destined to be saved

03:04.360 --> 03:07.000
Take flight! Right now!

03:07.000 --> 03:10.180
Pierce through all your loneliness!

03:10.180 --> 03:14.680
It hurts, it hurts doesn't it? Those tears are your overflowing dreams

03:14.680 --> 03:17.060
Come, flap your wings!

03:17.060 --> 03:21.160
The Alice girls are playing in the high skies

03:21.330 --> 03:25.760
Tell me! When you understood what it meant to believe,

03:25.760 --> 03:31.180
What was the colour of the sky above your plane?

03:32.580 --> 03:36.940
I just want to know

03:43.600 --> 03:43.990
Third

03:43.600 --> 03:44.270
Girls

03:43.850 --> 03:44.440
Fighter

03:44.270 --> 03:44.440
Wing

03:48.320 --> 03:49.690
Vector 32,

03:49.700 --> 03:51.200
We have a visual,

03:51.200 --> 03:53.280
We have confirmed Midway Pillar.

03:58.780 --> 04:01.450
So this is Midway Pillar...

04:01.460 --> 04:03.220
Amazing...

04:03.230 --> 04:05.420
Across the entire world, these things...

04:05.420 --> 04:07.660
The Builders are really something, aren't they...

04:09.160 --> 04:12.160
All units in Attack Team, this is Strike Leader.

04:12.160 --> 04:18.240
This operation will begin humanity's first opposition against the Builders.

04:18.240 --> 04:23.240
The objective is to retrieve the remaining survivors in the Midway Base.

04:23.240 --> 04:25.980
From the four years ago when they first appeared to now,

04:25.980 --> 04:29.880
It is now time to gain information on the all-mysterious Builders.

04:29.880 --> 04:33.880
We must ensure the success of this mission.

04:34.220 --> 04:39.350
As the Attack Team, our duty is to escort the rescue transport, Doggy Bag.

04:39.350 --> 04:43.140
And also to provide aerial support during the operation.

04:43.540 --> 04:45.780
It's expected to turn into a fierce battle, but,

04:45.780 --> 04:47.220
For the sake of this operation,

04:47.220 --> 04:49.940
Distinguished pilots from all over the world are here today.

04:49.940 --> 04:52.720
Those who overcame the calamity known as the "Great Lost",

04:52.720 --> 04:56.760
The champions who, despite their dated machines, held out in unfavorable battles.

04:56.760 --> 05:00.120
I believe that you will ensure the success of this mission.

05:00.450 --> 05:04.580
To reclaim the sky, and the technology, that was stolen from us,

05:04.580 --> 05:06.580
All units! Master Arm On!

05:08.000 --> 05:09.960
We have six enemies.

05:09.960 --> 05:11.120
Vector 34,

05:11.120 --> 05:13.120
Angel-1, Mach 1.3.

05:11.120 --> 05:13.120
Angel-1: altitude of  radar contact is 10,000 feet.

05:24.000 --> 05:25.400
Red-3, lost!

05:37.240 --> 05:38.920
Purple-1 and 2, lost!

05:39.640 --> 05:41.660
This is Doggy Bag.

05:41.660 --> 05:46.220
It’ll be two minutes before we begin the approach - but that's assuming we'll be in the air that long.

05:46.220 --> 05:48.520
Alice Leader to Doggy Bag.

05:48.530 --> 05:50.280
We shall escort you,

05:50.280 --> 05:51.640
Please rest assured.

05:51.940 --> 05:54.540
Roger, Alice Leader. We're counting on you!

05:54.720 --> 05:56.020
Please leave it to us!

05:56.020 --> 06:01.210
After all, we've got the most powerful sweep wing fighter on the planet, the MiG-23 with us!

06:01.220 --> 06:04.550
Woah there, old planes aren't cut out for this sort of thing!

06:04.550 --> 06:06.710
On that note the quality of my Kfir-

06:06.710 --> 06:08.780
A complete rip-off of the Mirage~

06:08.780 --> 06:09.590
Why you little!

06:09.590 --> 06:13.360
Hey, speaking of which, A-chan, what do you like about your F-1?

06:13.820 --> 06:15.020
Nothing in particular.

06:15.770 --> 06:17.760
Fighter planes are just tools after all.

06:17.770 --> 06:21.760
Bah, A-chan-senpai is still as uncaring as usual.

06:22.380 --> 06:23.660
Red-1, lost!

06:23.660 --> 06:25.660
It's no good, we're completely outmatched!

06:26.040 --> 06:27.830
If we could at least use a F-15...!

06:27.830 --> 06:32.760
There's no helping it. The engines from that era can't even start.

06:32.760 --> 06:33.990
However -

06:33.990 --> 06:36.410
Blue Leader! There are two bandits heading your way!

06:37.140 --> 06:39.360
Roger. Blue Leader engaging!

06:39.540 --> 06:40.060
-2

06:41.940 --> 06:48.500
However, "You'll go up against F-35's in a F-4" is something I'd love to try to tell my past self!

06:48.700 --> 06:52.300
Let's see who has the last laugh.

07:04.780 --> 07:06.250
Airspace clear!

07:06.260 --> 07:07.920
Runway, no problems.

07:07.920 --> 07:09.120
Doggy Bag - Acknowledged.

07:09.160 --> 07:10.640
Now commencing landing.

07:22.280 --> 07:24.920
This is Doggy Bag, we have successfully landed.

07:25.400 --> 07:27.980
The rescue team has begun their assault.

07:28.290 --> 07:29.810
Roger, Doggy Bag.

07:31.350 --> 07:33.340
Above you! AGM!

07:31.470 --> 07:33.340
AGM: Air-to-Ground Missiles

07:35.120 --> 07:36.840
Doggy Bag is...!

07:52.120 --> 07:54.780
Alice-4, engaging.

07:58.760 --> 08:00.180
A-chan-senpai!?

08:00.180 --> 08:02.080
Bugbear, what was that just now?

08:02.080 --> 08:06.960
Visual confirmed. 12-o'clock, high. Type 22, three of them, a new enemy.

08:07.770 --> 08:08.980
New enemies below as well:

08:08.980 --> 08:10.560
F-35s, three of them!

08:10.570 --> 08:13.500
A-chan can handle the upper ones. We've got these ones!

08:13.500 --> 08:15.300
Alice Leader, Engaging.

08:15.300 --> 08:16.220
-2

08:16.220 --> 08:16.940
-3

08:21.620 --> 08:23.560
Alice-4: Type 22 eliminated.

08:24.160 --> 08:25.210
Even more...

08:25.210 --> 08:26.940
Another one down.

08:26.940 --> 08:30.020
I thought Japan's F-1 was an attack aircraft, wasn't it?

08:30.020 --> 08:33.880
Yeah, it's kind of an assault type fighter plane,

08:33.880 --> 08:37.360
But it's just barely able to perform ACM.

08:33.880 --> 08:37.360
ACM: Air Combat Maneuvering

08:37.360 --> 08:39.180
Not to mention up against Raptors,

08:39.180 --> 08:40.700
Normally it would be suicide.

08:40.700 --> 08:42.200
So how...?

08:42.200 --> 08:44.820
She can spot enemies before the radar,

08:44.820 --> 08:47.810
She also has the reflexes to gun down AGM.

08:47.810 --> 08:51.480
Furthermore, even if her allies were picked off,

08:51.480 --> 08:53.960
She'll carry out the next maneuver with a cool head.

08:53.960 --> 08:56.540
It's like she has a heart made of ice.

09:02.140 --> 09:03.360
A third one!

09:03.360 --> 09:06.290
That's why everyone calls her that:

09:06.290 --> 09:08.360
"Ice Doll".

09:08.360 --> 09:10.410
As expected of A-chan-senpai~

09:10.410 --> 09:12.580
We can't lose to her now!

09:12.580 --> 09:14.390
Let's hurry up and clean up the rest!

09:14.400 --> 09:15.500
Roger!

09:15.800 --> 09:20.570
Doggy Bag to Bugbear. The assault team has recovered a survivor.

09:20.570 --> 09:23.760
I repeat, one survivor recovered!

09:23.760 --> 09:25.760
Presently extracting!

09:25.760 --> 09:27.160
Roger, Doggy Bag.

09:29.240 --> 09:30.360
A girl?

09:31.070 --> 09:32.360
Oi! Look out!

09:40.160 --> 09:41.520
Even in there!?

09:50.820 --> 09:52.220
Retreat!

09:52.220 --> 09:52.940
Run!

10:16.520 --> 10:19.540
Strike Leader to Doggy Bag, what happened!?

10:19.600 --> 10:22.700
This is Strike Leader, respond! Doggy Bag!

10:23.160 --> 10:26.980
Alice-4 to Strike Leader, Doggy Bag is down.

10:26.980 --> 10:28.500
Retrieval team - annihilated.

10:28.810 --> 10:30.140
The survivor?

10:30.140 --> 10:32.560
The recovered girl is still...

10:35.140 --> 10:36.640
I'll go check and retrieve her.

10:36.640 --> 10:37.480
Retrieve!?

10:37.490 --> 10:38.600
She intends to land!?

10:38.600 --> 10:40.480
That's reckless in this situation!

10:44.960 --> 10:48.290
A new Bogey! Type unknown. Entering Suppression Area!

10:48.290 --> 10:50.240
All units, to the Midway Base!

10:50.240 --> 10:51.920
Provide Alice-4 support!

10:51.920 --> 10:52.820
Roger!

11:46.480 --> 11:48.620
Alice-4, we'll hold this one off!

11:48.620 --> 11:49.920
Hurry up the retrieval!

11:56.720 --> 11:58.930
This guy just won't stay still.

12:09.480 --> 12:10.460
Myers!

12:18.580 --> 12:21.480
The enemy trumps us in both acceleration and mobility.

12:22.060 --> 12:22.740
Shit!!

12:23.700 --> 12:24.560
Olivia-san!

12:24.560 --> 12:25.640
Lieutenant Colonel!

12:25.640 --> 12:26.680
Are you alright?

12:26.820 --> 12:29.440
Could that be, an ATD-X!?

12:29.440 --> 12:33.600
Japan's 6th generation fighter plane, the amalgamation of the latest technology!

12:33.600 --> 12:36.500
If I recall, it should've still been in development!

12:36.800 --> 12:40.610
Are you telling me the Builders have even copied those cutting edge weapons!?

12:43.620 --> 12:46.220
Not good! It's heading towards Alice-4 again!

12:55.960 --> 12:59.240
Ouch, what're you doing! Geez...

13:05.940 --> 13:07.100
Eh, where are we?

13:07.100 --> 13:08.080
I'll explain later.

13:08.080 --> 13:08.960
Move!

13:08.960 --> 13:10.240
Where to?

13:15.480 --> 13:16.840
Wait, what's going on??

13:22.940 --> 13:23.620
It's coming.

13:23.800 --> 13:24.840
What is?

13:24.980 --> 13:25.860
Nothing of concern.

13:47.460 --> 13:49.960
W-w-w-w-we're gonna crash!

13:49.440 --> 13:50.240
Shut it!

14:02.560 --> 14:04.260
That was close.

14:04.500 --> 14:05.440
Not yet.

14:06.640 --> 14:08.440
It's not over yet!

14:12.080 --> 14:13.540
A-chan-senpai!

14:27.840 --> 14:29.260
Not good, I can't hit it!

14:29.260 --> 14:30.940
It's completely ignoring us!

14:31.040 --> 14:32.860
Stop ignoring us!

14:32.860 --> 14:33.800
This thing...

14:34.020 --> 14:35.440
No return fire.

14:35.780 --> 14:40.220
The Builders' machines are supposed to lock onto whatever attacks them...

14:41.090 --> 14:42.280
Why in the world...?

14:44.860 --> 14:48.440
Don't tell me... It's after that retrieved girl?!

15:27.940 --> 15:30.160
LIKE I'D LET YOU!!

16:01.000 --> 16:02.560
For the sake of the recovered,

16:02.560 --> 16:04.560
Alice-4: head towards Anderson AFB.

16:02.560 --> 16:04.560
Andersen AFB: US Air Force Base in Guam

16:04.840 --> 16:06.080
After reaching Ophelia,

16:06.080 --> 16:08.440
Wait for HQ's instructions on channel 13.

16:08.780 --> 16:11.480
This channel will now close. Over.

16:11.900 --> 16:13.600
Roger. Alice-4.

16:18.960 --> 16:21.480
Was that for real? That "Ice Doll"!

16:21.480 --> 16:25.680
Calmly making use of her comrade's explosion, who sacrificed herself to cover her...

16:25.680 --> 16:28.600
Is her heart really made of ice or something?

16:28.600 --> 16:33.360
Like I'd said, that's why she's known as "Ice Doll".

16:36.240 --> 16:40.220
Hey uh, why did they call you "Ice Doll"?

16:41.400 --> 16:43.360
Because I'm just like ice.

16:47.920 --> 16:50.840
I've already discarded my so called heart.

16:52.660 --> 16:53.540
Liar.

16:54.500 --> 16:58.640
I mean, during the fight you were crying the whole time weren't you?

16:59.540 --> 17:03.260
It hurts, it's painful - you were crying the whole time weren't you?

17:04.500 --> 17:09.360
Say, tell me, your real name.

17:10.260 --> 17:11.360
Aria.

17:12.700 --> 17:14.280
Hitotose Aria.

17:18.460 --> 17:20.180
Thanks, Aria.

17:20.520 --> 17:22.180
Thank you for saving me.

17:22.800 --> 17:27.340
For the unseen tears and blood you shed for my sake.

17:27.940 --> 17:29.960
I won't ever forget them.

17:35.060 --> 17:38.060
It's alright. Everything's going to be just fine, okay?

17:39.420 --> 17:41.620
So please, remember me as well, alright?

17:42.320 --> 17:46.020
I'm...eh?

17:46.740 --> 17:48.340
Wait, you're kidding.

17:48.660 --> 17:50.980
Say Aria, who am I?

17:51.480 --> 17:53.060
This has to be a joke!

17:53.060 --> 17:54.900
Are you saying that I have-

17:54.900 --> 17:56.900
Memory loss?

17:58.760 --> 18:04.400
EEEEEEEEEEEEEHHHH????

18:07.080 --> 18:09.660
"It is that which, four years ago,

18:09.970 --> 18:12.360
Appearing suddenly all throughout the globe,

18:12.800 --> 18:16.320
Disrupted the function of all electronics:

18:16.820 --> 18:18.320
"Great Lost".

18:18.440 --> 18:22.920
Gigantic structures have been built all over the world, one after another.

18:23.320 --> 18:27.140
These mysterious constructions, made by what is now known as "Builders",

18:27.140 --> 18:28.820
Are still being built.

18:28.820 --> 18:34.160
One third of the world has now been covered by the outer layer assembled by the Builders."

18:36.460 --> 18:37.760
Well, well, well.

18:37.760 --> 18:41.280
I was worried there for a bit, but seems like we managed.

18:41.640 --> 18:44.080
Thank you, Rear General Lye.

18:44.480 --> 18:47.000
We don't need to scrap the craft now.

18:47.060 --> 18:49.580
I mean, under current circumstances,

18:49.620 --> 18:52.360
Anything that's usable should really get fixed.

18:52.360 --> 18:53.760
Hold up there.

18:54.100 --> 18:58.960
I'd prefer if you did not forget about the parts gathered by us remnants of the Clow Corporation.

19:00.100 --> 19:02.560
Commander Valroph, a call from Kansai.

19:03.520 --> 19:06.060
Pansai's requesting to land at this base.

19:07.060 --> 19:08.420
Give the OK.

19:08.730 --> 19:13.080
After that, notify Christine to gather all the pilots in the briefing room.

19:13.080 --> 19:13.680
Yes Ma'am!

19:16.880 --> 19:18.640
Chofu Base

19:29.040 --> 19:30.440
Commander Valroph!

19:30.440 --> 19:31.940
Present arms!

19:31.940 --> 19:32.780
Order arms!

19:34.980 --> 19:36.380
At ease.

19:37.300 --> 19:40.180
Today our 307 Fighter Squadron,

19:40.180 --> 19:43.880
Will have a new pilot introduced into our ranks.

19:44.320 --> 19:45.540
Excuse me~

19:50.820 --> 19:54.660
New on the base today, Catherine Weller - Second Lieutenant. Reporting for duty!

19:55.060 --> 19:56.040
This girl is?

19:56.040 --> 19:59.700
The mysterious girl rescued by Second Lieutenant Aria.

20:00.120 --> 20:02.040
She herself wished it,

20:02.040 --> 20:04.040
So we're taking her into our care at this base.

20:04.200 --> 20:06.840
Please, call me Cathy without reserve!

20:07.020 --> 20:09.720
B-but, didn't she have amnesia?

20:09.820 --> 20:12.460
Ah, isn't that great! Got your memories back already, huh?

20:12.460 --> 20:14.860
No, unfortunately that isn't the case yet.

20:14.980 --> 20:17.900
For some reason I can remember how to pilot a plane,

20:17.900 --> 20:19.260
But elsewise... Not a clue!

20:19.260 --> 20:21.480
Not having a name woulda been inconvenient,

20:21.580 --> 20:23.700
So I just gave myself one~

20:23.900 --> 20:27.080
By the way, Second Lieutenant Cathy will be living with Aria.

20:27.440 --> 20:29.980
Therefore, be sure to look after her for a while.

20:30.660 --> 20:31.960
I'll be in your care~

20:35.600 --> 20:38.480
A-chan, Ari-chan, Acchan..?

20:38.760 --> 20:41.480
Mmm... None of those click...

20:41.560 --> 20:43.480
Hey, what should I call you?

20:44.680 --> 20:45.960
Do as you wish.

20:46.340 --> 20:48.020
Then.. Crybaby-chan!

20:50.520 --> 20:51.840
Just messing with you~

20:53.540 --> 20:55.000
Can I call you Aria?

20:57.060 --> 20:58.740
Do as you wish...

20:59.980 --> 21:01.860
Umm, Second Lieutenant Catherine?

21:01.980 --> 21:03.160
Cathy~

21:03.160 --> 21:05.560
C...Cathy?

21:05.660 --> 21:06.900
What is it, Aria?

21:07.380 --> 21:10.400
Have your memories really not come back yet?

21:10.410 --> 21:12.710
Do Not Use

21:10.600 --> 21:14.160
Yeah, but boy was I surprised after hearing about lots of things!

21:14.160 --> 21:17.880
That "Great Lost" which was quickly brought about by the "Builders"?

21:17.880 --> 21:23.320
And that all the latest fighter planes and all the computers were rendered inoperable.

21:24.580 --> 21:28.440
Of the planes which can still move, the 1970s is the limit.

21:28.440 --> 21:31.240
Those from the 80's and later are basically useless, right?

21:31.600 --> 21:34.880
For the most part. Only up to Third Generation Fighter Jets.

21:34.920 --> 21:39.600
In comparison, Builders can copy all our cutting edge tech.

21:40.020 --> 21:41.900
Talk about a mission impossible!

21:46.000 --> 21:47.220
We've arrived.

21:47.780 --> 21:48.460
Yes.

21:51.780 --> 21:54.580
So, it's fine to let her sortie normally, right?

21:56.500 --> 21:58.360
Understood, your Excellency.

22:00.940 --> 22:03.640
It feels sooo goooood~~~

22:03.820 --> 22:07.060
Having just gotten off the plane, this is pure bliss!

22:07.300 --> 22:11.240
Wouldn't it be the best if we could take a dip in a giant bath afterwards~

22:11.240 --> 22:13.520
Lots of hot water all the way up to the shoulders~

22:13.540 --> 22:16.300
I wanna taste that unbridled feeling of relaxation!

22:16.400 --> 22:19.520
Hey, are you really American?

22:19.520 --> 22:21.780
The doctor said that that's probably the case~

22:21.840 --> 22:26.100
To Tatiana, it seems that Cathy-san was in the mood to make a Japanese style remark!

22:27.200 --> 22:29.960
So, do you think you'll get used to the base?

22:30.060 --> 22:31.160
Of course!

22:31.800 --> 22:34.300
How about you, A-chan? Think you'll be able to have fun?

22:34.620 --> 22:35.520
I...

22:35.520 --> 22:37.700
There's no doubt we'll have a blast! Right?

22:38.440 --> 22:42.540
C-C-Cathy! Those.. roun-

22:43.520 --> 22:44.940
Hmm, what about these?

22:44.940 --> 22:47.680
They only get in the way during battles~

22:49.860 --> 22:52.340
Aww, you're just so adorable~

22:52.620 --> 22:55.320
This is my first time seeing A-chan-senpai like this!

22:55.320 --> 22:56.260
Same here.

22:56.470 --> 23:00.360
After seeing a face like that, no one would be calling her "Ice Doll".

23:01.640 --> 23:03.440
Attention, attention.

23:03.440 --> 23:05.780
Message from the National Alliance HQ.

23:05.780 --> 23:09.100
Enemy fleet approaching from Abashiri, Hokkaido.

23:09.100 --> 23:10.560
Entering FAST PACE security.

23:09.100 --> 23:12.700
FAST PACE: Alert security level on the verge of highest alert severity. (DEFCON 2).

23:10.560 --> 23:12.700
I repeat, entering FAST PACE security!

23:12.740 --> 23:17.170
Flighter squadrons 307, 401, 405, immediate takeoff

23:13.160 --> 23:14.880
Move out!

23:17.280 --> 23:21.620
It seems like the enemy are planning to infiltrate Honshuu from Abashiri.

23:22.080 --> 23:27.020
The B-1B loaded with a Pillar Seed is being escorted toward our direction.

23:27.400 --> 23:30.380
Misawa scrambled planes to intercept, but

23:30.500 --> 23:32.640
We're also to provide reinforcements.

23:33.020 --> 23:35.800
We cannot allow them to erect a pillar on Honshuu.

23:35.820 --> 23:37.800
Stop them at all costs!

23:40.000 --> 23:41.720
Let's go, everyone!

23:41.860 --> 23:42.640
Yeah!!

24:15.120 --> 24:21.230
"I wont fly anymore" is a terribly lonely thing for you to say

24:21.230 --> 24:27.350
You see, even now you hold the skies within your eyes

24:27.350 --> 24:30.720
It's so sad that tears won't even flow

24:30.720 --> 24:34.090
If you're living in such a past

24:34.090 --> 24:39.760
That's even more the reason to return to the skies!

24:39.760 --> 24:45.960
In a corner of an uncertain, isolated world

24:45.960 --> 24:52.600
Whilst trembling alone, you're waiting for the time when your journey begins

24:52.600 --> 24:53.880
Halation!

24:53.880 --> 24:56.960
Spreading your wings transcends time and space

24:56.960 --> 25:04.720
Before long you'll be carried beyond the dreams you've been longing for

25:04.720 --> 25:09.130
And at that time, you'll come to understand what it means to believe

25:09.130 --> 25:16.110
So don't be afraid! You can fly, and keep on flying!

25:16.110 --> 25:20.730
To the heavens!

25:22.190 --> 25:25.590
And then you will have...

25:28.360 --> 25:31.120
seen the sky.
